    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Heat exposure has an adverse effect on the health of pregnant women and newborns which is affecting timely access and utilisation of health services, particularly in rural communities in sub-Saharan Africa, according to a study conducted by the Climate Health and Maternal Neonatal Health Africa (CHAMNHA) project in Kaloleni and Rabai sub-counties in Kilifi County between February and April 2021.",
